{
  "name": "Child Worker Workflow",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔧 CHILD WORKER WORKFLOW\n\n**Role:** Contains all the business logic.\n\n**Principle:** Fail-Fast — if something goes wrong, the node fails immediately and returns the error to the Controller (Parent) without handling exceptions locally.\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Receives the payload from the Parent\n2. Formats the data\n3. Calls the external API (CRM, ERP, etc.)\n4. Returns the result to the Parent\n\n\n⚠️ Do **NOT** add any error handling logic here.",
        "height": 408,
        "width": 380,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "5b1280ec-5099-4c45-b17a-8aaa7828966a",
      "name": "📋 CHILD WORKER — Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -48
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Trigger\n\nReceives the payload sent by the **Execute Sub-workflow** node in the Parent.\n\nData arrives as a standard JSON item and is immediately available via `$json`.",
        "height": 288,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "21c2748c-d930-46d2-a354-b222783e0eb6",
      "name": "📌 Step 1 — Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        432,
        -48
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Format Data\n\nPerforms transformation and normalization of the payload before sending it to the external API.\n\nAdds useful metadata such as timestamp and worker ID for traceability.",
        "height": 288,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "81b9f60b-b519-4605-b38e-6b0bb9f8bb6c",
      "name": "📌 Step 2 — Format Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        768,
        -48
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## HTTP Request\n\nSimulates a call to an external CRM, ERP, or Payment Gateway.\n\n🔴 **This node can fail** (timeout, rate limit, 500 error). In that case the entire workflow terminates with an error, which is caught by the Controller.\n\n➡️ Replace the URL with your real endpoint.",
        "height": 292,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "7b461247-a93e-4fb6-a504-d62f6c216a4e",
      "name": "📌 Step 3 — HTTP Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1104,
        -48
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Response to Parent\n\nReturns the processed result to the Controller.\n\nThe Parent uses this response in the **success branch** to continue the normal flow.",
        "height": 294,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "fe80e2c8-6a45-41b0-a637-e6da1c4594d7",
      "name": "📌 Step 4 — Respond",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1440,
        -48
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
